/// Singleton settings row holding the Billing v2 master switch. Mirrors
/// attendance_settings' SHAPE (scope='GLOBAL' + rolloutStage) but is a SEPARATE
/// table on purpose: Billing's rollout must be pullable without touching the
/// attendance gate, and attendance_settings carries 20+ unrelated policy knobs.
///
/// `rolloutStage` is 'OFF' | 'TEST_USERS_ONLY' | 'ALL_USERS' — the same union as
/// auth.config.ts's RolloutStage. Enforced live by a CHECK constraint
/// (chk_billing_settings_rollout_stage), which Prisma cannot express — do NOT
/// try to model it. `scope` is UNIQUE (billing_settings_scope_key): that is what
/// keeps this a singleton and what the seed's ON CONFLICT targets.
///
/// Created by hand in the Supabase SQL Editor and hand-mirrored here — db pull
/// cannot run on this machine (CORE §3). Do NOT db push/pull.
model billing_settings {
  id           Int      @id @default(autoincrement())
  scope        String   @default("GLOBAL")
  rolloutStage String   @default("OFF")
  updatedAt    DateTime @updatedAt @db.Timestamptz(6)
  updatedById  Int?
  updatedBy    users?   @relation("BillingSettingsUpdatedBy", fields: [updatedById], references: [id])

  @@unique([scope])
}

